// reply.rs
pub fn generate_reply(input: &str) -> String {
    if input.trim().is_empty() {
        return String::from("Fine. Be that way!");
    } else if input.ends_with('?') {
        return String::from("Sure.");
    } else if input.to_uppercase() == input && input.chars().any(|c| c.is_alphabetic()) {
        return String::from("Whoa, chill out!");
    } else {
        return String::from("Whatever.");
    }
}
```

The solution defines the `reply` module and its `generate_reply` function as specified. The `generate_reply` function analyzes the input string based on the given conditions and returns the appropriate reply. The `trim` method is used to handle empty or whitespace-only input. The `ends_with` method checks for a question mark at the end of the input. The `to_uppercase` method is used to check for all capital letters, and the `chars` iterator is used to verify if the input contains any alphabetic characters. The function returns the corresponding reply based on the input analysis.

