fn can_eliminate_copy(bb: &BasicBlock, copy_src: Register, copy_dst: Register) -> bool {
    let l = &bb.liveness_ref();
    !l.live_in.contains(&copy_dst)
        && !l.live_out.contains(&copy_dst)
        && !l.live_in.contains(&copy_src)
        && !l.live_out.contains(&copy_src)
}
```
The `can_eliminate_copy` function checks the liveness information of the basic block `bb` to determine whether the given register copy can be eliminated. It returns `true` if both the source and destination registers are not live at the same time, indicating that the copy operation is unnecessary and can be eliminated.

