```rust
fn count_function_sections(webasm: &[u8]) -> usize {
    let mut count = 0;
    let mut offset = 0;

    while offset < webasm.len() {
        if webasm[offset] == 0x03 {
            count += 1;
        }
        let payload_len = leb128_decode(&webasm[offset + 1..]);
        offset += 1 + payload_len as usize;
    }

    count
}

fn leb128_decode(bytes: &[u8]) -> u32 {
    let mut result = 0;
    let mut shift = 0;
    let mut byte_index = 0;

    loop {
        let byte = bytes[byte_index];
        result |= ((byte & 0x7F) as u32) << shift;
        if (byte & 0x80) == 0 {
            break;
        }
        shift += 7;
        byte_index += 1;
    }

    result
}
```

In the solution, the `count_function_sections` function iterates through the WebAssembly binary data, identifying function sections by their opcode (0x03) and counting them. The `leb128_decode` function is used to decode the LEB128-encoded payload length of each section. The count of function sections is then returned.

