    for line in comment.lines() {
        if line.trim_start().starts_with("///") {
            let content = line.trim_start_matches("///").trim();
            if content.starts_with("#") {
                let attribute = content.trim_start_matches("#").trim();
                attributes.push(attribute.to_string());
            } else {
                if !description.is_empty() {
                    description.push_str(" ");
                }
                description.push_str(content);
            }
        }
    }

    (attributes, description)
}
```

The `parse_documentation_comment` function iterates through each line of the input comment, checks for attributes and extracts the description. It trims the lines, checks for attributes starting with `#`, and appends the description accordingly. The extracted attributes and description are returned as a tuple.

